Like James wrote, I typically use the following line <https://github.com/wibeasley/Wats/blob/master/UtilityScripts/Refresh.R#L10> to to inspect the documentation closely
system("R CMD Rd2pdf --force --output=./DocumentationPeek.pdf ." )

And instead of deleting the file, I include a line in the .Rbuildignore <https://github.com/wibeasley/Wats/blob/master/.Rbuildignore#L6> file so the build process doesn't produce a warning.  I like being able to look at the reference manual without having to install the package.

There have also been a few times that the development version's manual has information that SAS users wanted to see; at that point it's really nice to post the GitHub link <https://github.com/LiveOak/NlsyLinksStaging/blob/master/NlsyLinks/NlsyLinksDocumentationPeek.pdf>.

